WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:06.560
Since the original "The Fast and the Furious"&nbsp;
in 2001, each film in the franchise has added&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:12.240
more names onto the roster. With two decades&nbsp;
worth of Fast films and more on the way, that's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:17.840
a lot of faces and backstories to remember. So&nbsp;
we've recapped every main character's story,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.840 --> 00:00:23.040
including where they started, where they are now,&nbsp;
and any notable stops they've made along the way.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:28.400
When we meet Dominic Toretto in "The Fast and the&nbsp;
Furious," he's helping his sister, Mia run their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:33.920
family's small L.A. market, while also running&nbsp;
an operation stealing electronics off moving&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.920 --> 00:00:40.560
18-wheelers and participating in illegal street&nbsp;
races. Dom was once incarcerated for assaulting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:46.160
the man he blamed for causing the accident that&nbsp;
killed his father. However, that wasn't enough&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.160 --> 00:00:50.960
to steer him away from crime, which eventually&nbsp;
led to him going on the run to avoid arrest.

00:00:50.960 --> 00:00:55.040
Dom's been with his girlfriend, Letty, since&nbsp;
they were teenagers. They eventually marry&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.040 --> 00:00:59.520
in the fourth film, although their wedding&nbsp;
isn't revealed until the seventh. In between,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.520 --> 00:01:05.360
when Dom's forced to flee justice again, he learns&nbsp;
Letty's been killed. After taking time to grieve,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.360 --> 00:01:10.400
he dates Elena Neves, fathering a child with&nbsp;
her, although he doesn't learn about his son's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.400 --> 00:01:15.920
existence until months after he's born. While&nbsp;
Elena's pregnant, he learns Letty's alive but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.920 --> 00:01:20.240
suffering from amnesia. Elena steps aside&nbsp;
so they can be together. Eventually,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.240 --> 00:01:23.600
Letty regains her memories,&nbsp;
and, following Elena's death,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:27.760
Letty and Dom raise his son together,&nbsp;
whom Dom names after his best friend.

00:01:28.320 --> 00:01:31.600
"Everyone, meet Brian."

00:01:32.720 --> 00:01:35.200
After many films spent evading justice,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:40.720
Dom's taste for crime increases over the course&nbsp;
of the series, although he tends to target greedy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.720 --> 00:01:46.800
corporations and corrupt crime lords. But&nbsp;
the most valuable thing to him is family,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.800 --> 00:01:50.800
specifically the crew he's assembled to&nbsp;
help him pull off his various schemes.

00:01:51.360 --> 00:02:00.640
"The most important thing in life will always be&nbsp;
the people in this room. Right here, right now."

00:02:01.440 --> 00:02:05.200
In "Fast and Furious 6," Dom and his&nbsp;
crew partner with the government to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:09.280
bring down various terrorists, earning&nbsp;
them full pardons for their past crimes.

00:02:10.240 --> 00:02:14.560
Introduced in "The Fast and the Furious,"&nbsp;
undercover LAPD officer Brian O'Conner&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.560 --> 00:02:19.760
initially ingratiates himself with Dom under&nbsp;
false pretenses. His goal is to earn Dom's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.760 --> 00:02:24.640
trust so that he can catch him and his crew&nbsp;
in the act and arrest them all. But gradually,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.640 --> 00:02:29.680
his friendship with Dom turns genuine, and&nbsp;
Brian ultimately chooses Dom over his career.

00:02:29.680 --> 00:02:35.280
Brian goes underground but is found by the FBI,&nbsp;
who offer him a deal: bring down drug lord Carter&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.280 --> 00:02:41.200
Verone and get pardoned. Brian agrees, and joins&nbsp;
the FBI. Later, he sends Letty undercover with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:46.240
cartel leader Arturo Braga, but later learns&nbsp;
she's been killed. To track down her killer,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.240 --> 00:02:51.440
he reunites with Dom, as well as Dom's sister,&nbsp;
Mia, whom Brian briefly dated years before.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.440 --> 00:02:56.240
When Dom kills Letty's supposed murderer and&nbsp;
earns himself a lifelong prison sentence,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.240 --> 00:02:59.840
Brian ditches his career again&nbsp;
to partner with Mia and free him.

00:02:59.840 --> 00:03:05.440
Later, when Mia tells Brian she's pregnant, Brian&nbsp;
and Dom decide to pull off one last heist that'll&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.440 --> 00:03:10.880
allow them to drop off the grid and live in peace.&nbsp;
But Brian is pulled back to crime twice more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.880 --> 00:03:16.080
after that — once, when Dom learns that Letty's&nbsp;
alive, and again when their crew is targeted by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.080 --> 00:03:21.920
a terrorist. Finally, with a second baby on the&nbsp;
way, Brian decides to step away from the fast,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.920 --> 00:03:26.560
furious lifestyle for good, settling&nbsp;
down with Mia and his growing family.

00:03:26.560 --> 00:03:30.400
Off-screen, Brian was written out of the&nbsp;
franchise because of Paul Walker's sudden&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.400 --> 00:03:35.280
death during production of "Furious 7." While&nbsp;
Mia can still return as part of the crew,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.280 --> 00:03:40.560
Brian's story is complete, with his character&nbsp;
last seen driving off happily into the sunset.

00:03:42.036 --> 00:03:45.520
Letty Ortiz has long been&nbsp;
Dom's partner in everything,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:45.520 --> 00:03:50.320
sticking by him even when Dom keeps leaving&nbsp;
her behind. After he goes on the run at the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.320 --> 00:03:54.160
end of "The Fast and the Furious," Letty&nbsp;
spends several years tracking him down,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:54.160 --> 00:03:58.240
eventually finding him in the Dominican&nbsp;
Republic. Picking up where they left off,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.240 --> 00:04:03.600
the couple wastes no time in secretly marrying&nbsp;
before pulling their biggest heist yet. But&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:03.600 --> 00:04:08.000
when the plan goes sideways, Dom goes on the&nbsp;
run, once again leaving Letty on her own.

00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:09.840
Letty brokers a deal with Brian:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:09.840 --> 00:04:13.600
She'll go undercover to help bring down&nbsp;
Braga in exchange for Dom's pardon.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:13.600 --> 00:04:18.080
But when she uncovers a plot to kill her,&nbsp;
she tries to flee, only to be left for dead.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:18.080 --> 00:04:23.200
Eventually Letty awakens in the hospital with&nbsp;
amnesia, and is taken in by criminal Owen Shaw.

00:04:23.200 --> 00:04:27.600
Letty works for years as part of Shaw's&nbsp;
crew, with no memory of her former life,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:27.600 --> 00:04:32.640
but switches sides when she encounters Dom and&nbsp;
he wins her trust. The two date for a while,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.640 --> 00:04:36.640
but Letty breaks up with him, because she doesn't&nbsp;
think they should be together while she still&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.640 --> 00:04:41.040
lacks her memories. However, she regains&nbsp;
them when Dom's nearly killed, and the two&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:41.040 --> 00:04:46.160
finally take their long-overdue honeymoon.&nbsp;
Even when Dom appears to betray the team after&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:46.160 --> 00:04:52.295
being blackmailed, Letty never loses faith, and&nbsp;
welcomes him back into the family with open arms.

00:04:52.295 --> 00:04:56.000
"You know I never left you, Letty."
"I know."

00:04:56.000 --> 00:04:57.280
"And you know I never will."

00:04:59.760 --> 00:05:01.219
"I know."

00:05:01.360 --> 00:05:05.200
Mia Toretto resisted her brother's criminal&nbsp;
endeavors for a long time, but she's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:05.200 --> 00:05:09.280
eventually pulled in when Dom is sentenced&nbsp;
to prison and she helps Brian break him out.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:09.280 --> 00:05:13.920
After that, Mia sticks with Brian as they travel&nbsp;
internationally and pull off daring heists.

00:05:13.920 --> 00:05:18.720
When they're double-crossed by a crime lord named&nbsp;
Reyes, Brian and Dom believe they'll need to split&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:18.720 --> 00:05:24.560
up to avoid being caught. Mia disagrees, revealing&nbsp;
she's pregnant. The trio instead decide to recruit&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:24.560 --> 00:05:30.320
a crew to steal $100 million of Reyes' money so&nbsp;
that they can go underground and live in peace.

00:05:30.320 --> 00:05:35.040
Once the heist is complete, Mia and Brian&nbsp;
settle down in the Canary Islands. There,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:35.040 --> 00:05:39.920
she gives birth to their son, Jack. Afterward,&nbsp;
she agrees that Brian should help Dom&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:39.920 --> 00:05:44.000
find Letty while she stays with Jack,&nbsp;
but she gets kidnapped by Owen Shaw.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:44.000 --> 00:05:49.920
After being freed, just as Mia realizes she's&nbsp;
expecting their second child, their house blows&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:49.920 --> 00:05:55.680
up. Brian joins Dom for one final mission,&nbsp;
and once their family is finally safe again,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:55.680 --> 00:06:00.160
Mia and Brian retire for good. However,&nbsp;
Mia will be rejoining the action — this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:00.160 --> 00:06:05.920
time without Brian — when her estranged&nbsp;
older brother Jakob shows up in "F9."

00:06:06.640 --> 00:06:11.600
Roman Pearce started stealing cars at a young&nbsp;
age. But when his friend Brian O'Conner joined&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:11.600 --> 00:06:18.080
the LAPD, Roman grew resentful, especially when&nbsp;
Brian did nothing to help when Roman was arrested.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:18.080 --> 00:06:23.360
The two reconnect in "2 Fast 2 Furious," when&nbsp;
Brian recruits Roman to help in an investigation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:23.360 --> 00:06:28.400
requiring them to go undercover. In return,&nbsp;
the FBI promises them both a pardon. They&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:28.400 --> 00:06:33.360
complete their mission and clear their names,&nbsp;
and recover a large amount of stolen money.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:33.360 --> 00:06:39.520
Unbeknownst to the FBI, though, Roman also sets&nbsp;
aside a generous portion of the cash for himself.

00:06:39.520 --> 00:06:44.080
Roman re-enters the picture in "Fast Five,"&nbsp;
when Brian and Dom need someone on their team&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:44.080 --> 00:06:49.520
who can talk his way out of any situation.&nbsp;
After pocketing $11 million from that heist,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:49.520 --> 00:06:54.480
Roman lives lavishly, buying expensive cars&nbsp;
and a private jet, but still rejoins the crew&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:54.480 --> 00:06:59.920
whenever he's needed. He helps Dom find Letty and&nbsp;
foil both Shaw brothers, and sticks around after&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:59.920 --> 00:07:05.280
Brian retires. When Dom seems to betray the crew&nbsp;
while being blackmailed by Cipher, Roman is part&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:05.280 --> 00:07:10.000
of the group that works to stop him, and is quick&nbsp;
to welcome him back once the truth is revealed.

00:07:11.440 --> 00:07:17.440
Introduced in "2 Fast 2 Furious," super-mechanic&nbsp;
Tej meets Brian O'Conner while Brian is living&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:17.440 --> 00:07:20.960
in Miami, and the two become friends&nbsp;
through the street racing scene. Later,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:20.960 --> 00:07:24.640
Tej assists Brian and Roman in&nbsp;
their undercover FBI assignment.

00:07:24.640 --> 00:07:29.280
Brian brings Tej back in for the heist in&nbsp;
"Fast Five," using his tech skills to hack&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:29.280 --> 00:07:33.600
into Reyes' advanced security system. Tej&nbsp;
also becomes close to Roman, although the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:33.600 --> 00:07:38.640
two never miss an opportunity to get under each&nbsp;
other's skin. From "Fast Five" on, Tej works&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:38.640 --> 00:07:43.840
as an integral part of the crew, working as the&nbsp;
team's mechanic, hacker, and occasional driver.

00:07:44.720 --> 00:07:50.320
Only appearing in "2 Fast 2 Furious," Suki is a&nbsp;
street racer with a mostly female crew of her own.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:50.320 --> 00:07:55.360
She is friends with Brian and Tej, and proves&nbsp;
a valuable asset when Roman and Brian need help&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:55.360 --> 00:08:00.080
throwing the police off their scent. While&nbsp;
Tej drives Brian's car, Suki drives Roman's,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:00.080 --> 00:08:03.760
leading the police on a wild goose&nbsp;
chase away from their actual targets.

00:08:04.640 --> 00:08:10.000
A significant character in "2 Fast 2 Furious,"&nbsp;
Monica Fuentes is an undercover U.S. Customs&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:10.000 --> 00:08:15.040
agent who's working to expose Miami drug lord&nbsp;
Carter Verone. When Brian and Roman are also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:15.040 --> 00:08:20.160
embedded in the operation, Monica blows her cover&nbsp;
to pass Brian important information. Realizing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:20.160 --> 00:08:24.880
Monica's betrayal, Verone takes her hostage&nbsp;
aboard his boat, but Brian and Roman distract&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:24.880 --> 00:08:29.440
him long enough for Monica to take advantage of&nbsp;
the situation. She holds Verone at gunpoint until&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:29.440 --> 00:08:34.240
she's able to arrest him. Several years later,&nbsp;
she alerts Hobbs that Letty is still alive.

00:08:35.280 --> 00:08:40.720
Ex-Mossad agent Gisele is introduced as an&nbsp;
employee of Arturo Braga in the fourth film.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:40.720 --> 00:08:45.040
However, Gisele warns Dom that Braga&nbsp;
plots to kill his drivers. Later,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:45.040 --> 00:08:50.800
Dom saves Gisele's life, then recruits Gisele in&nbsp;
"Fast Five" as an official member of his crew.

00:08:50.800 --> 00:08:51.760
"I think I'm in love."

00:08:52.640 --> 00:08:57.520
After becoming a couple in "Fast Five," Gisele&nbsp;
and Han are in Hong Kong together when they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:57.520 --> 00:09:02.320
receive Dom's call to come help stop Shaw&nbsp;
and save Letty in the sixth film. Tragically,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:02.320 --> 00:09:06.560
toward the end of the film, Gisele is hanging&nbsp;
off the top of a speeding car when she sees one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:06.560 --> 00:09:12.480
of Shaw's henchmen preparing to kill Han. Making&nbsp;
a split-second call, Gisele releases her grip on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:12.480 --> 00:09:16.800
Han's hand in order to kill his attacker,&nbsp;
saving his life as she falls to her death.

00:09:17.520 --> 00:09:21.760
Han got his start in director Justin Lin's&nbsp;
earlier film, "Better Luck Tomorrow."&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:21.760 --> 00:09:25.360
In high school, Han was part of an&nbsp;
organized cheating operation that spun&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:25.360 --> 00:09:30.000
out of control and eventually resulted in a&nbsp;
murder. Following the events of that film, Han&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:34.720
left to travel the world. He met Dom in Mexico,&nbsp;
and occasionally helped with various missions.

00:09:34.720 --> 00:09:38.960
Han's first appearance is in the third film,&nbsp;
but chronologically, his first mission is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:38.960 --> 00:09:44.640
in the fourth released film in the franchise,&nbsp;
which serves as a prequel to the third. Quiet,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:44.640 --> 00:09:50.800
observant, and adaptable, Han helps with Dom's&nbsp;
heists in the fourth, fifth, and sixth movies,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:50.800 --> 00:09:54.960
during which he also falls in love with&nbsp;
fellow crew member Gisele. The two dream&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:54.960 --> 00:10:00.000
of globe-trotting and growing old together, but&nbsp;
those plans are dashed when Gisele sacrifices&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:04.800
herself to save Han while working to take down&nbsp;
Owen Shaw. Grieving, Han heads to Tokyo, where&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:04.800 --> 00:10:09.600
he befriends a group of local street racers and&nbsp;
takes American teen Sean Boswell under his wing.

00:10:09.600 --> 00:10:13.840
Han also begins stealing from the Yakuza,&nbsp;
eventually finding himself in a high-speed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:13.840 --> 00:10:18.720
chase once his crimes are discovered. The chase&nbsp;
ends in a horrific crash, but it turns out to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:18.720 --> 00:10:23.920
no accident — Han was targeted by Owen's brother,&nbsp;
Deckard Shaw. It appears Han dies in the crash,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:23.920 --> 00:10:30.240
but "F9" reveals that, somehow, Han actually&nbsp;
survived and will rejoin Dom's crew.

00:10:31.280 --> 00:10:35.680
The youngest protagonist in the franchise, Sean&nbsp;
Boswell appears in "The Fast and the Furious:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:35.680 --> 00:10:39.520
Tokyo Drift" as an Alabama teen with&nbsp;
a penchant for reckless driving.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:39.520 --> 00:10:43.520
After being sent to Tokyo to live with his&nbsp;
father, Sean quickly falls in with the city's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:43.520 --> 00:10:48.480
street racing scene. But the Japanese racers&nbsp;
all know how to "drift" — maneuvering around&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:48.480 --> 00:10:53.520
tight corners via controlled skids — a skill&nbsp;
which Sean is initially unable to master.

00:10:53.520 --> 00:10:58.400
Han takes Sean under his wing and teaches&nbsp;
him how to drift. Sean also flirts with a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:58.400 --> 00:11:02.480
girl that turns out to be the girlfriend of&nbsp;
Takashi, the local Drift King and the nephew&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:02.480 --> 00:11:07.040
of a Yakuza member. After Han's apparently&nbsp;
killed while being pursued by the Yakuza,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:07.040 --> 00:11:11.680
Sean challenges Takashi to a race, with&nbsp;
the loser agreeing to leave Tokyo for good.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:11.680 --> 00:11:16.720
Thanks to Han's teaching, Sean beats&nbsp;
Takashi, and is crowned the new Drift King.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:16.720 --> 00:11:20.760
Afterward, he meets Dom while Dom is&nbsp;
in Tokyo investigating Han's death.

00:11:21.760 --> 00:11:25.120
An American army brat, Twinkie&nbsp;
eventually landed in Tokyo,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:25.120 --> 00:11:29.280
selling stolen goods out of Han's garage.&nbsp;
He met Sean Boswell in high school,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:29.280 --> 00:11:33.040
and they become friends after they&nbsp;
bond over Twinkie's unique car.

00:11:33.040 --> 00:11:36.720
Through Twinkie, Sean is introduced to&nbsp;
Han and the Tokyo street racing crowd.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:36.720 --> 00:11:40.800
And when Sean finds himself on the wrong&nbsp;
side of the Yakuza after Han's death,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:40.800 --> 00:11:45.280
Twinkie even gives him money to pay off his debts.&nbsp;
The two remain friends at the end of the movie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:45.280 --> 00:11:48.480
with Twinkie serving as the second&nbsp;
in command to the new Drift King.

00:11:49.200 --> 00:11:54.320
Originally serving as a secondary antagonist in&nbsp;
"Fast Five," Luke Hobbs enters the picture as a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:54.320 --> 00:11:58.480
Diplomatic Security Service agent tasked&nbsp;
with tracking down the crew. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:58.480 --> 00:12:03.680
after finally getting the upper hand and arresting&nbsp;
Dom, Brian, and several members of their crew,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:03.680 --> 00:12:08.720
Hobbs' caravan is ambushed. When Dom, Brian,&nbsp;
and their friend Vince save Hobbs' life,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:08.720 --> 00:12:14.320
he decides to join them to get revenge. After the&nbsp;
mission is complete, Hobbs returns to the DSS,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:14.320 --> 00:12:20.000
where he learns Letty Ortiz is alive. Hobbs passes&nbsp;
this intel to Dom, and after Dom's crew assists&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:20.000 --> 00:12:25.280
in tracking Letty down and capturing Owen Shaw,&nbsp;
Hobbs is able to negotiate pardons for everyone.

00:12:25.280 --> 00:12:30.320
Hobbs is later injured when Deckard Shaw breaks&nbsp;
into the DSS in search of information on the crew,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:30.320 --> 00:12:35.840
but still helps bring Shaw to justice. Later, when&nbsp;
Hobbs is tasked with an off-the-books mission,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:35.840 --> 00:12:40.160
he calls on Dom and his crew to help him.&nbsp;
But Dom's double-cross for Cipher winds up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:40.160 --> 00:12:44.640
sending Hobbs to prison. He breaks out&nbsp;
and helps the team stop Cipher. Later,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:44.640 --> 00:12:49.760
Hobbs is tasked by the CIA with teaming up with&nbsp;
Deckard Shaw to recover a dangerous bioweapon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:49.760 --> 00:12:53.200
which leads to him reconnecting&nbsp;
with his estranged family in Samoa.

00:12:54.800 --> 00:12:58.640
We meet Elena in "Fast Five," when&nbsp;
she's recruited by Hobbs to assist&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:58.640 --> 00:13:02.000
in his investigation. But when&nbsp;
she comes face to face with Dom,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:02.000 --> 00:13:07.200
she opts not to shoot him when she has the&nbsp;
chance. In turn, Dom saves her from Reyes' men,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:07.200 --> 00:13:11.520
making Elena question whether he could really&nbsp;
be guilty of the crimes he's accused of.

00:13:11.520 --> 00:13:16.480
After Dom and Brian save her life again, Elena&nbsp;
leaves her law enforcement career to go on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:16.480 --> 00:13:20.880
run with Dom. The two begin a relationship&nbsp;
on the Canary Islands, where she also grows&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:20.880 --> 00:13:26.320
close to Brian and Mia. But when Dom learns&nbsp;
Letty's alive, Elena urges him to find her.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:26.320 --> 00:13:32.240
Elena stays behind to protect Mia and baby Jack,&nbsp;
getting Jack to safety when Mia's kidnapped. After&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:32.240 --> 00:13:37.680
Dom finds Letty, Elena steps aside — not&nbsp;
revealing she's pregnant with Dom's child.

00:13:37.680 --> 00:13:43.120
Eventually, after joining the DSS with Hobbs,&nbsp;
Elena gives birth in secret. Shortly after,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:43.120 --> 00:13:47.520
she and her infant son are kidnapped by&nbsp;
Cipher to use as leverage against Dom.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:47.520 --> 00:13:52.720
Elena tells Dom she's given the baby a middle&nbsp;
name — Marcos — but she wanted Dom to choose&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:52.720 --> 00:13:58.560
his first name. Elena is soon executed by&nbsp;
Cipher as punishment for Dom's insubordination.

00:14:00.160 --> 00:14:04.800
We meet Vince in "The Fast and the Furious"&nbsp;
as a loyal member of Dom's crew who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:04.800 --> 00:14:10.000
instantly distrusts Brian. Part of Vince's&nbsp;
issue with Brian is Mia's attraction to him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:10.000 --> 00:14:12.320
since Vince wants her attention for himself.

00:14:12.320 --> 00:14:16.080
When the crew's heist goes drastically&nbsp;
wrong at the end of the first film,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:16.080 --> 00:14:21.120
Vince is seriously injured, prompting Brian to&nbsp;
blow his cover to get Vince medical attention.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:21.120 --> 00:14:25.920
At some point after his recovery, Vince goes&nbsp;
on the run, winding up in Rio de Janeiro, where&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:25.920 --> 00:14:31.040
he meets the woman who'd eventually become his&nbsp;
wife and mother of his son. After spending years&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:31.040 --> 00:14:36.640
resenting Brian, Vince ultimately forgives him&nbsp;
when he returns in "Fast Five." He offers shelter&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:36.640 --> 00:14:42.480
to Brian and Mia and rejoins the crew. Tragically,&nbsp;
he's killed by Reyes' men when they attack Hobbs,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:42.480 --> 00:14:47.360
so Dom gives Vince's portion of the $100&nbsp;
million heist to Vince's wife and son.

00:14:48.880 --> 00:14:52.240
Owen Sha16_w turned mercenary after&nbsp;
being dishonorably discharged from the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:52.240 --> 00:14:56.800
military. He became an associate of Arturo&nbsp;
Braga, which is how he met Letty Ortiz,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:56.800 --> 00:15:00.800
intending to finish her off after Braga's&nbsp;
initial attempt to kill her failed.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:00.800 --> 00:15:04.240
But instead he recruited Letty&nbsp;
as part of his criminal crew.

00:15:04.240 --> 00:15:08.720
After Braga's arrest, Shaw begins stealing&nbsp;
components to build an advanced weapon of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:08.720 --> 00:15:12.960
mass destruction, which he intends to&nbsp;
sell off to the highest bidder. He acts&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:12.960 --> 00:15:18.160
ruthlessly, willingly sacrificing members of&nbsp;
his crew and kidnapping Mia to use as leverage&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:18.160 --> 00:15:23.920
to secure his freedom. He's ultimately stopped&nbsp;
by Dom and is grievously injured in the process.

00:15:23.920 --> 00:15:27.120
After being hospitalized for&nbsp;
an extended period of time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:27.120 --> 00:15:31.280
Owen is transferred to a secret location.&nbsp;
While being blackmailed by Cipher,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:31.280 --> 00:15:35.520
Dom makes a deal with Shaw's mother to find&nbsp;
him in exchange for her family's assistance,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:35.520 --> 00:15:41.040
to which she agrees. Owen, then, is instrumental&nbsp;
in helping rescue Dom's baby from Cipher.

00:15:42.160 --> 00:15:47.120
Introduced in "Fast &amp; Furious 6" as a&nbsp;
DSS agent and associate of Luke Hobbs,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:47.120 --> 00:15:51.920
Riley Hicks is an ex-soldier with an impressive&nbsp;
record. She works alongside Hobbs to track down&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:51.920 --> 00:15:57.600
Owen Shaw and his team, and is helpful in both&nbsp;
combat and extracting information from informants.

00:15:57.600 --> 00:16:02.640
However, after Dom's group helps Hobbs arrest&nbsp;
Shaw, Riley reveals she's been a double agent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:02.640 --> 00:16:07.920
the whole time, and is romantically involved with&nbsp;
Shaw. From that point on, Riley is openly a part&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:07.920 --> 00:16:13.760
of Shaw's crew, and proves willing to kill for him&nbsp;
in cold blood. Riley is ultimately killed by Letty&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:13.760 --> 00:16:18.000
when Letty shoots her with a harpoon gun, causing&nbsp;
her to fall from Shaw's plane to her death.

00:16:19.520 --> 00:16:24.960
Although Brian and Dom spent most of "Fast &amp;&nbsp;
Furious" working for the drug lord known as Braga,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:24.960 --> 00:16:29.440
it turns out the man they thought was Braga&nbsp;
was actually a decoy. The real Braga was his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:29.440 --> 00:16:34.240
second-in-command, who'd gone by the name Ramon&nbsp;
Campos. Those closest to him knew about the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:34.240 --> 00:16:40.240
deception, but everyone else bought into the lie,&nbsp;
helping the real cartel leader avoid detection.

00:16:40.240 --> 00:16:43.840
For a while, this helps him fly&nbsp;
under Brian and Dom's radar. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:43.840 --> 00:16:48.720
they're eventually able to apprehend him in&nbsp;
Mexico, and he's sentenced to life in prison.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:48.720 --> 00:16:53.520
At some point prior to this, though, he formed&nbsp;
an alliance with Owen Shaw, who helped influence&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:53.520 --> 00:16:58.160
Braga's operation, and whom Braga hired&nbsp;
to kill Letty. While Braga's in prison,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:58.160 --> 00:17:02.000
Brian poses as a prisoner to get close to&nbsp;
him in order to find out more information&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:02.000 --> 00:17:06.560
about what happened to Letty. Braga tells&nbsp;
him everything before attempting to kill him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:06.560 --> 00:17:10.480
but Brian manages to get the upper hand,&nbsp;
stabbing Braga in the leg in the process.

00:17:11.920 --> 00:17:16.720
Leo and Santos are friends of Dom's from his&nbsp;
time in the Dominican Republic. The pair are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:16.720 --> 00:17:22.080
instrumental in helping Dom plan and execute the&nbsp;
fuel heist at the beginning of the fourth film,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:22.080 --> 00:17:26.640
and reappear at the end of the film to&nbsp;
help Brian and Mia break Dom out of prison.

00:17:26.640 --> 00:17:30.000
After receiving their cut of their&nbsp;
multimillion-dollar score at the end&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:30.000 --> 00:17:35.360
of "Fast Five," Santos and Leo head to a casino,&nbsp;
where they wager all their money playing roulette.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:35.360 --> 00:17:40.160
We never learn who wins or loses, but they show&nbsp;
up again later in "The Fate of the Furious"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:40.160 --> 00:17:44.480
as part of Dom's plan to fake Deckard's&nbsp;
death, proving they still have Dom's trust.

00:17:45.120 --> 00:17:50.320
Introduced in the fourth film, F.B.I. agent&nbsp;
Michael Stasiak initially gets along with Brian,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:50.320 --> 00:17:54.240
but the two butt heads when Stasiak&nbsp;
brings Mia in for questioning. After&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:54.240 --> 00:17:58.880
Brian tricks him into letting her go, Stasiak&nbsp;
is suspicious of Brian's loyalties. He winds&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:58.880 --> 00:18:03.600
up second-guessing him at a critical juncture&nbsp;
that puts their undercover operation at risk.

00:18:03.600 --> 00:18:06.720
However, Stasiak still has a good&nbsp;
enough impression of Brian to help&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:06.720 --> 00:18:11.280
him sneak back into the U.S. in "Fast&nbsp;
&amp; Furious 6." He then gives Brian an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:11.280 --> 00:18:15.680
alias and embeds him in the prison where&nbsp;
Braga's being kept so Brian can question him.

00:18:16.400 --> 00:18:21.040
First introduced21 in "Furious 7," Ramsey's&nbsp;
an accomplished hacker who catches the crew's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:21.040 --> 00:18:25.360
attention after she invents a device called&nbsp;
the God's Eye, which can be used to track&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:25.360 --> 00:18:30.560
down anyone on the planet. Realizing how&nbsp;
dangerous the God's Eye can be, Ramsey sends&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:30.560 --> 00:18:35.040
it to a friend to keep safe, but she's then&nbsp;
kidnapped by a mercenary seeking the device.

00:18:35.040 --> 00:18:39.920
Knowing Deckard Shaw has targeted Dom's crew, the&nbsp;
government strikes a bargain: If Dom retrieves&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:39.920 --> 00:18:44.960
Ramsey and the God's Eye, he can use it to&nbsp;
track down Shaw. After the crew rescues Ramsey,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:44.960 --> 00:18:50.480
she helps them track down the God's Eye and defeat&nbsp;
Shaw. She eventually joins Dom's crew permanently.

00:18:51.360 --> 00:18:56.080
Owen's brother Deckard first appears at the&nbsp;
end of "Fast &amp; Furious 6," tracking down&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:56.080 --> 00:19:01.040
and presumably killing Han in Tokyo. A&nbsp;
former clandestine military operative&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:01.040 --> 00:19:06.720
and MI6 agent turned mercenary, Deckard uses&nbsp;
his skills to break into the DSS offices&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:06.720 --> 00:19:11.760
and steal information on Dom's team. While&nbsp;
he's in Tokyo, he also mails a bomb to Dom's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:11.760 --> 00:19:17.040
childhood home, where Mia and Brian are living,&nbsp;
and detonates it while on the phone with Dom.

00:19:17.040 --> 00:19:22.080
Deckard continues his attempts to hunt and kill&nbsp;
the crew, but he's ultimately thwarted by Dom&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:22.080 --> 00:19:27.920
and taken into CIA custody. Hobbs is later put&nbsp;
into the cell opposite him, and the two waste no&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:27.920 --> 00:19:33.200
time in annoying each other. But before long, the&nbsp;
pair escape during a prison riot, initiated by Mr.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:33.200 --> 00:19:38.480
Nobody, a covert government agent. Reluctantly,&nbsp;
Deckard agrees to work with Dom's crew to stop&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:38.480 --> 00:19:43.760
Cipher, since he also blames her for Owen's fate.&nbsp;
After helping them track down Dom and Cipher,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:43.760 --> 00:19:48.960
it appears Deckard is killed by Dom, but that's&nbsp;
revealed to be a ruse facilitated by his mother.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:48.960 --> 00:19:52.960
With Owen, Deckard breaks onto&nbsp;
Cipher's plane and rescues Dom's son,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:52.960 --> 00:19:58.160
whom he returns safely to Dom. Later, Deckard's&nbsp;
recruited by the CIA to assist Hobbs — to their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:58.160 --> 00:20:02.800
mutual irritation — in recovering a bioweapon&nbsp;
possessed by Deckard's sister, Hattie.

00:20:03.760 --> 00:20:07.040
Although Cipher isn't introduced&nbsp;
until "The Fate of the Furious,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:07.040 --> 00:20:11.520
she's been pulling strings behind the scenes&nbsp;
for quite some time. She hired Owen Shaw to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:11.520 --> 00:20:16.720
steal the components he was assembling in "Fast&nbsp;
&amp; Furious 6," and was the mastermind behind the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:16.720 --> 00:20:21.440
plan to steal the God's Eye in "Furious 7."&nbsp;
It's even implied she has ties to Braga.

00:20:21.440 --> 00:20:26.560
In the eighth movie, Cipher kidnaps Elena and&nbsp;
her son to use as leverage to manipulate Dom,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:26.560 --> 00:20:31.600
which works for a while. However, while Cipher&nbsp;
knows that Dom's loyalty lies with his family,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:31.600 --> 00:20:34.560
she underestimates how far&nbsp;
he'll go to keep them safe,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:34.560 --> 00:20:37.600
enabling him to eventually&nbsp;
break free of her control.

00:20:37.600 --> 00:20:41.280
Motivated by power, Cipher's&nbsp;
goal is to start a nuclear war.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:41.280 --> 00:20:44.240
Even though her plans are thwarted&nbsp;
by the end of the eighth movie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:44.240 --> 00:20:48.320
she manages to escape, and will be&nbsp;
returning to collect her revenge in F9.

00:20:49.680 --> 00:20:53.920
No one knows Mr. Nobody's real name,&nbsp;
or even which government organization&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:53.920 --> 00:20:58.480
he works for. All we know is that he's a&nbsp;
covert agent who shows up in "Furious 7"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:58.480 --> 00:21:02.800
offering Dom the chance to track down&nbsp;
Deckard Shaw in exchange for his assistance.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:02.800 --> 00:21:09.680
Describing himself as a "shadow," Mr. Nobody has&nbsp;
abundant resources and technology at his disposal,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:09.680 --> 00:21:13.280
and is untethered by official&nbsp;
policies and procedures.

00:21:13.280 --> 00:21:17.360
Mr. Nobody shows up again in "The Fate&nbsp;
of the Furious," staging a prison riot&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:17.360 --> 00:21:21.440
to free Hobbs and Shaw so that they can&nbsp;
help Dom's crew track down their leader.

00:21:21.440 --> 00:21:26.320
Meanwhile, Little Nobody shows up as Mr.&nbsp;
Nobody's protégé in "The Fate of the Furious."

00:21:26.320 --> 00:21:27.200
"So then who's he?"

00:21:27.200 --> 00:21:28.800
"Him? He's nothing. He's like less than me."

00:21:29.680 --> 00:21:34.080
While not on the level of most of Dom's&nbsp;
crew, Little Nobody still participates in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:34.080 --> 00:21:37.440
the high-speed effort to stop Cipher&nbsp;
from launching a nuclear submarine.

00:21:38.880 --> 00:21:43.680
We first meet Shaw family25_ matriarch Magdalene&nbsp;
in "The Fate of the Furious," when Dom sneaks&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:43.680 --> 00:21:48.400
away from Cipher long enough to ask her for&nbsp;
help. Dom offers Queenie a deal — in exchange&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:48.400 --> 00:21:53.680
for her help rescuing his infant son, he will&nbsp;
give her the location of her incarcerated son,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:53.680 --> 00:21:59.840
Owen. The trade is acceptable to Magdalene,&nbsp;
who, like Dom, values family above all else.

00:21:59.840 --> 00:22:03.440
Sometime later, Queenie goes to&nbsp;
prison, although we never learn why.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:03.440 --> 00:22:07.600
But at the end of "Hobbs and Shaw," it's implied&nbsp;
that she's getting ready to break herself out,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:07.600 --> 00:22:11.840
thanks to a nail file hidden in a cake&nbsp;
delivered to her by Deckard and Hattie.

00:22:12.400 --> 00:22:19.600
We don't know much about Jakob, who'll debut in&nbsp;
"F9." But what we do know indicates he'll be very&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:19.600 --> 00:22:24.880
different from the other Toretto siblings. Dom and&nbsp;
Mia have never mentioned Jakob, and maybe there's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:24.880 --> 00:22:30.160
a good reason for that. The ninth "Fast and the&nbsp;
Furious" film will see Jakob teaming with Cipher&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:30.160 --> 00:22:35.840
to take down his big brother, which may prove&nbsp;
to be the biggest challenge Dom has ever faced.

00:22:35.840 --> 00:22:38.640
Jakob is a skilled assassin and, of course,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:38.640 --> 00:22:42.400
an excellent precision driver. We'll&nbsp;
learn what happened to set the Toretto&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:42.400 --> 00:22:46.560
siblings at one another's throats when&nbsp;
"F9" finally speeds into theaters.

